{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Then you shall take an awl.</b> I have explained it. The reason for mentioning this is that you are obligated to give him [gifts] when he goes free; only if he does not wish to go free, you shall pierce his ear." "<b>And likewise to your maidservant you shall do.</b> It is joined with 'you shall furnish him liberally' (Deuteronomy 15:14). If it is far, like 'he shall surely pay' — [שלם ישלם being an infinitive absolute construction] — if he does not have. And if [these are] three [cases], and many [authorities] say thus, for a woman is not pierced."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The lemma 'באזנו ובדלת' in the source text does not match the verse's 'ולקחת את המרצע ונתתה באזנו ובדלת'; rendered the actual Hebrew lemma as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:37.995649470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}